# Gradle / Java
.gradle/
build/
out/
*.class
*.jar
# A pattern with a slash anchors at the repository root, and the wrapper jars
# live under mod/gradle/ and forge/gradle/ — the unanchored form here used to
# cover a root gradle/ that does not exist, so a re-added wrapper jar would be
# silently ignored and a clean clone's ./gradlew would not run (BUILD-1).
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
# The shipped mod jar is a release artifact, not a build output. Without this the
# `*.jar` rule above silently drops it from dist/ and the release workflow fails
# its own checksum gate on a file that is listed but not there.
!dist/*.jar

# The release zip is a build product of scripts/package.sh, fully redundant with
# dist/ (the workflow zips dist/ itself). It was once committed at 2.4 MB.
/blockreality-*.zip

